      "message": "I\u0027ll keep that in mind since next time, thank you (I\u0027m not properly used to do informative git commits, i apologise for that). And I\u0027ll try to explain in very best way I can. Anyways, the cost comes from libutils/binder/RefBase.cpp. In RefBase, the explicit destruction only logs a one-line ALOGW and is guarded only by if ANDROID_UTILS_CALLSTACK_ENABLED (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android-14.0.0_r75:system/core/libutils/binder/RefBase.cpp;l\u003d793). It\u0027s the full native unwind and symbolization that I was talking about. It does exist in the current android 16 as well (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android-latest-release:system/core/libutils/binder/RefBase.cpp;l\u003d804;). In the same RefBase.cpp file, on a14, on lines 58-65, the android_utils_callstack_enabled is defined and on a16, it\u0027s defined on lines 59-66. __linux__ makes it default to one. But only difference occurs in libutils/binder/Android.bp, as you pointed out on line 56 which only appears in libutils_binder_sdk. But, in a16, there is no any flags in the defaults chain that actually builds the platform libutils. which is (libutils_binder_impl_defaults_nodeps_no_apex \u003e _nodeps \u003e _defaults \u003e libutils_binder).\nThis is not by any LLM either, i just want to explain as properly as I understood it.",
